ich had not lost this event in over a decade at major internationals. Britain was expected to be formidable in Rio, but the USA had " [:a {:href "/athletes/93860"} "Michael Phelps"] " back, and a rejuvenated " [:a {:href "/athletes/103585"} "Ryan Lochte"] ", and was the favorite."] "\n\n" [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/126671"} "Conor Dwyer"] " put the USA in the lead in the final, posting 1:45.23 to lead Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/120876"} "Kosuke Hagino"] ", with Great Britain in fifth place on the first leg. On the second leg, American " [:a {:href "/athletes/136370"} "Townley Haas"] " swam 1:44.14 and effectively ended the gold medal battle, giving the USA almost a three-second lead, with Lochte and Phelps yet to swim. Those two swam effectively but were never pushed, and they never pushed it, the USA winning gold in 7:00.66, with Britain in second, 2½ seconds behind, and just edging out Japan for the silver medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "7:06.74 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "7:00.66 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "10"} [:a {:href "/athletes/93860"} "Michael Phelps"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/103585"} "Ryan Lochte"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/126671"} "Conor Dwyer"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/136356"} "Clark Smith"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/136359"} "Gunnar Bentz"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/136360"} "Jack Conger"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/136370"} "Townley Haas"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Great Britain"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"}